.TH AGENT-HOOK-PRE-MCP 1 "2026-06-30" "agentguard" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
agent-hook-pre-mcp \- guard agent MCP tool calls before execution
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B agent-hook-pre-mcp
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B agent-hook-pre-mcp
reads an MCP hook JSON payload from standard input. It blocks MCP servers after
repeated failures, warns on expensive or under-scoped MCP calls, and then lets
local extensions add environment-specific MCP policy.
.PP
After three consecutive failures of one server, calls to it are blocked
until 60 seconds have passed since the last failure or retry probe. Then
the next call goes through as a probe:
.BR agent-hook-post-mcp (1)
closes the breaker if it succeeds and restarts the cooldown if it fails.
The block message reports the seconds until the next probe and quotes the
last failing tool and the start of its error, noting that repeated failures
are often bad arguments rather than an unavailable server; after two failed
probes it says the server is probably down.
.PP
The base policy warns on exact
.B search_files
leaf-tool calls without a path filter and warns once on exact
.B knowledge_load
leaf-tool calls because large documents can consume significant context.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The MCP call is allowed, possibly with warnings.
.TP
.B 2
The MCP call is blocked. AgentGuard internal errors also block.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR agent-hook-post-mcp (1)
